OL,3,GNEWSA'One of Britain's rarest birds
OL,4,Awalked past my kitchen window'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman spotted one of the UK's rarest
OL,7,Fand most elusive birds in her garden in
OL,8,Fwhat has been described as an "almost
OL,9,Fexceptional" sighting.
OL,11,FKarine Nohr saw the juvenile bittern as
OL,12,Fit strolled past the kitchen window of
OL,13,Fher home in Nether Edge, Sheffield,
OL,14,Fbefore wandering into her back garden
OL,15,Fand attempting to fish in her pond.
OL,17,FBitterns, which live in wetlands and
OL,18,Fmake a distinctive booming noise, were
OL,19,Fconsidered an extinct breeding bird in
OL,20,FYorkshire in 1997 but numbers have
OL,21,Fsince made a recovery due to habitat
OL,22,Fmanagement.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
